{% comment %}
  Step 1 of 5 — "Choose your concern". New step inserted between Entry and
  Doctor Select: after choosing "Book a consultation" on Entry, the visitor
  picks a concern here first, THEN moves on to picking a doctor.
  Explicit instruction: this only applies to the consultation path — Therapy
  Slot's flow is untouched.

  Inserting this as step 1 pushed every downstream step's progress
  dots/label down by one (Doctor Select 1/5->2/5, Slot Picker 2/5->3/5,
  Patient Details 3/5->4/5) — Confirmation was already 5/5 (last of 5) so it
  needed no change. See kal-booking-flow.js's goToStep comment / each step's
  own header for the renumbering.

  This step is a structured replacement for a free-text "what are you
  coming in for" field, not a doctor filter/search — so each row is just an
  icon + name + checkbox, no doctor count. Selecting a concern doesn't
  filter the Doctor Select list that follows; it still shows its same
  doctor list regardless of what's picked here.

  MOBILE REDESIGN (this file, this pass): a new Figma spec replaced the
  original single-select/radio version with:
  - Multi-select checkboxes instead of a single radio (see
    kal-booking-flow-concern-row.liquid and kal-booking-flow.js's
    concernSelect Set)
  - A new, larger category list (General Wellness, Bone/Joint/Muscle Pain,
    Gut Health, PCOS/PCOD/Menopause, Skin/Hair, Diabetes/Thyroid/BP,
    Reproductive Health/Infertility, Liver/Kidney Health) replacing the old
    medical-specialty names
  - The "Not sure?" banner moved from the footer to right under the title
  - A location badge (facility name only, no working dropdown — explicit
    instruction: "for now dont need this dropdown just the selected
    facility should be shown here") in place of the progress dots in the
    mobile header, with a separate "STEP 1 OF 5 / Next: Mode & Doctor" bar
    + progress bar underneath
  - A floating down-chevron scroll hint over the list

  Explicit instruction: THIS PASS IS MOBILE-ONLY. The desktop composition
  (progress dots in the header, no step-bar, no scroll hint) is
  deliberately left exactly as it was — every new element below is hidden
  at 750px+, and the pre-existing desktop elements are hidden below 750px
  instead of removed. See kal-booking-flow.css's own comment on this
  step for exactly which classes do which.

  ICON GAP, flagged rather than silently worked around: only 7 'concern-*'
  icons exist (kal-booking-icons.liquid), all named after the OLD
  specialty list. The new categories reuse the closest existing icon where
  one genuinely fits (Bone/Joint/Muscle Pain -> orthopedics, Gut Health ->
  gastroenterology, PCOS/PCOD/Menopause and Reproductive Health/Infertility
  -> gynecology). Skin/Hair, Diabetes/Thyroid/BP, and Liver/Kidney Health
  have no reasonable existing match — marked below with a REUSED ICON
  comment each, using the nearest available icon as a placeholder. Real
  icons for these three need to be added to kal-booking-icons.liquid before
  this should be considered final.

  Single shared markup, not a __mobile + __desktop split — see the "SHARED
  STEP SHELL" comment in kal-booking-flow.css for why and how the layout
  switches at 750px.
{% endcomment %}

<div class="kal-step-concern-select kal-step-shell">

  <div class="kal-step-entry__info kal-step-shell__info">
    <div class="kal-step-entry__info-content">
      <h2 class="kal-step-entry__heading">Choose your concern</h2>
      <p class="kal-step-entry__body-text">
        We&rsquo;ll match you with available doctors. Book a consultation
        in under a minute in-clinic or video.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="kal-step-entry__location">
      <span class="kal-icon kal-icon--location">
        <!-- ICON: location-pin (not received yet) -->
      </span>
      <span class="kal-step-entry__location-text">
        Kerala Ayurveda Wellness Center, Indiranagar &middot; Opens 8 AM
      </span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="kal-step-shell__panel">

    <div class="kal-step-doctor-select__header kal-step-shell__header">
      <button type="button" class="kal-step-doctor-select__back" data-kal-back="entry" aria-label="Back">
        {%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'chevron-left' -%}
      </button>

      <div class="kal-concern-select__header-middle">
        {%- comment -%}
          Mobile: static facility badge. The chevron is shown per the
          updated Figma spec (a plain rotated chevron-left, same trick the
          spec itself uses — "chevron_left" rotated -90deg — rather than a
          separate down-chevron icon), but it's purely visual: no
          data-kal-facility hook, no click handler. Explicit instruction:
          "dont need this dropdown [behavior] just the selected facility
          should be shown" — the chevron stays for visual match, the
          dropdown it implies doesn't actually open anything yet.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <div class="kal-concern-select__location-badge">
          <span class="kal-concern-select__location-badge-left">
            <span class="kal-icon kal-icon--location">
              {%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'location-pin' -%}
            </span>
            <span class="kal-concern-select__location-text">Indiranagar</span>
          </span>
          <span class="kal-concern-select__location-chevron" aria-hidden="true">
            {%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'chevron-left' -%}
          </span>
        </div>

        {%- comment -%} Desktop: unchanged progress dots, hidden below 750px, see CSS {%- endcomment -%}
        <div class="kal-step-doctor-select__progress">
          <span class="kal-step-doctor-select__progress-dot kal-step-doctor-select__progress-dot--active"></span>
          <span class="kal-step-doctor-select__progress-dot"></span>
          <span class="kal-step-doctor-select__progress-dot"></span>
          <span class="kal-step-doctor-select__progress-dot"></span>
          <span class="kal-step-doctor-select__progress-dot"></span>
          <span class="kal-step-doctor-select__progress-text">1/5</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      {%- comment -%} Own close button — see Doctor Select's header comment for why {%- endcomment -%}
      <button type="button" class="kal-step-doctor-select__back" data-kal-close aria-label="Close">&times;</button>
    </div>

    {%- comment -%} Mobile-only step-bar, replaces the header's progress dots visually at this width — see CSS {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="kal-concern-select__step-bar">
      <div class="kal-concern-select__step-bar-labels">
        <span class="kal-concern-select__step-bar-step">Step 1 of 5</span>
        <span class="kal-concern-select__step-bar-next">Next : Mode &amp; Doctor</span>
      </div>
      <div class="kal-concern-select__step-bar-track">
        <div class="kal-concern-select__step-bar-fill"></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="kal-step-shell__scroll">
      <div class="kal-step-doctor-select__intro">
        <h2 class="kal-step-doctor-select__heading">Choose your concern</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="kal-concern-select__banner">
        <span class="kal-icon kal-icon--info">
          {%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'info' -%}
        </span>
        <span class="kal-concern-select__banner-text">Not sure? <strong>General Wellness</strong> will guide you from there.</span>
      </div>

      <div class="kal-concern-select__list">
        {%- render 'kal-booking-flow-concern-row', icon_name: 'concern-general-medicine', name: 'General Wellness', concern_key: 'general-wellness', selected: false -%}
        {%- render 'kal-booking-flow-concern-row', icon_name: 'concern-orthopedics', name: 'Bone, Joint, Muscle Pain', concern_key: 'bone-joint-muscle-pain', selected: false -%}
        {%- render 'kal-booking-flow-concern-row', icon_name: 'concern-gastroenterology', name: 'Gut Health', concern_key: 'gut-health', selected: false -%}
        {%- render 'kal-booking-flow-concern-row', icon_name: 'concern-gynecology', name: 'PCOS, PCOD, Menopause', concern_key: 'pcos-pcod-menopause', selected: false -%}
        {%- comment -%} REUSED ICON — no dedicated skin/hair icon exists yet, using general-medicine as a placeholder {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- render 'kal-booking-flow-concern-row', icon_name: 'concern-general-medicine', name: 'Skin, Hair', concern_key: 'skin-hair', selected: false -%}
        {%- comment -%} REUSED ICON — no dedicated diabetes/thyroid/BP icon exists yet, using cardiology as the closest placeholder (BP) {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- render 'kal-booking-flow-concern-row', icon_name: 'concern-cardiology', name: 'Diabetes, Thyroid, BP', concern_key: 'diabetes-thyroid-bp', selected: false -%}
        {%- render 'kal-booking-flow-concern-row', icon_name: 'concern-gynecology', name: 'Reproductive Health, Infertility', concern_key: 'reproductive-health-infertility', selected: false -%}
        {%- comment -%} REUSED ICON — no dedicated liver/kidney icon exists yet, using gastroenterology as the closest placeholder {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- render 'kal-booking-flow-concern-row', icon_name: 'concern-gastroenterology', name: 'Liver, Kidney Health', concern_key: 'liver-kidney-health', selected: false -%}
      </div>
    </div>

    {%- comment -%}
      Mobile-only floating scroll hint — purely visual, signals more
      concerns below without needing a click handler. Positioned relative
      to the panel so it stays fixed near the bottom regardless of scroll
      position. Hidden at 750px+, see CSS.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="kal-concern-select__scroll-hint" aria-hidden="true">
      {%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'chevron-right' -%}
    </div>

    <div class="kal-step-shell__footer">
      <button type="button" class="kal-step-doctor-select__continue" data-kal-goto="doctor-select" data-kal-concern-continue disabled>
        Continue
      </button>
    </div>

  </div>

</div>
